Backlog item
Feature: Online payment authorised with Secure2u through the MAE app with MAE app PIN or biometric authentication.

Agile User Stories
1. As a Maybank customer, I want to be able to approve an online payment from my registered device only, so that scammers cannot approve fraudulent payments from my account even if they have access to my messages and card details.

| attributes\story | Story 1 |
|---|---|
| Independent | Partly, the story needs device registration to be built first but the approval requirements and constraints are independent of the implementation of device registration. |
| Negotiable | Yes, the story gives the developers flexibility on how to let the user approve their payment. |
| Valuable | Yes, the story prevents scammers from approving online payments by only allowing customers' registered device to approve them. |
| Estimable | Yes, the work can be estimateed based on the approval rule. However, it is unknown how each device indentified so this is treated as an assumption. |
| Small | Yes, the story is only for the approval of the payment from a registered device and does not include device registration. | 
| Testable | Yes, the feature can be tested by two scenarios: <br> 1. Triggering a payment and then approving a payment from a registered device and the payment goes through <br> 2. Triggering a payment and not approving it (since scmmaer does not have the registered device to approve it) and the payment gets cancelled |

2. As a Maybank customer, I want another option to approve an online payment that does not require me to enter my MAE app PIN, so that no one nearby can watch me enter it when I am approving in public.

| attributes\story | Story 2 |
|---|---|
| Independent | Partly, this is would be an optional method of approving online payment from Story 1, so device registration and Story 1 must be done first. |
| Negotiable | Yes, this story gives the developer flexibility on how to let user approve their online payment as long as it does not require MAE app PIN.  |
| Valuable | Yes, the feature provides privacy to customers when approving an online payment in public. |
| Estimable | Yes, the feature is straightforward enough to be estimated as the app only requests biometric authentication from the device. What is not known from the story is how many failed attempt is provide before it triggers PIN fallback  |
| Small | Yes, this feature is simple because it only request its own biometric authentication from the operating system so the authentication happens on the device itself rather than on Maybank's server  | 
| Testable | Yes, the feature can be tested by three scenarios: <br> 1. Approval is done with the alternative method without using PIN. <br> 2. Approval with alternatife method fails and would require PIN to be typed in. <br> 3. Approval requires PIN to be typed in because alternative method is not set up. |


